// Oracle instrumentation (work package P0.5, design/reference-build.md section 8).

#pragma once

// How the IClient logging proxy (oracle_iclient_proxy.cpp, generated by
// make_oracle_iclient.py) records each argument type of rpc_iclient.h that is not a scalar.
// One overload per type; make_oracle_iclient.py refuses a type that has none, so a new
// IClient argument type needs a line here and a body in oracle_iclient_args.cpp.
//
// Three kinds of record:
//   * plain structs with no pointer or container inside: "hex" bytes of sizeof(T), padding
//     included as the caller left it;
//   * structs that hold containers or pointers: an object of the fields that can be read
//     without the sender's state (counts, ids, the elements of arrays the struct points to);
//   * types whose content the client cannot measure here (FmtStr, CCharacterSet, CDAPacket):
//     the string "present".

